# The standard A/B profile: 40 stars (2 real, 38 made up), about 100 s on an Apple M1 (estimated as for quick.wu, not
# measured), long enough that three rounds give a median worth comparing and that the stub's 60 s checkpoint interval
# passes once. The production threshold (50 pc, scripts/make_work_units.py) means `out` holds only the two real stars
# and the `# done 40` trailer, as most real work units do, so a change that skips work on far stars shows its gain here
# and a change that wrongly drops a star shows as a missing row. Its output check is weak (two rows): use quick.wu for
# arithmetic. The same star_seed as quick.wu, so these stars start with quick.wu's.
iso oumuamua
stars 40
anchors 2
star_seed 20261104
seed_base 1
time_myr -100
steps 100000
threshold_pc 50
apps cpu
